record legeos.papercut.lege-doctor-exited-1-on-every-developer-install/1 : papercut {
    title "`lege doctor` exited 1 on every developer install and made…"
    state verified
    statement """
        `lege doctor` exited 1 on every developer install and made scripts/reinstall-legeos-desktop.sh refuse a perfectly good session. Two checks asked image-time questions at runtime: os-release demanded ID=legeos on an Ubuntu build host, and mime-handlers resolved handlers against LegeOS app manifests only, so all 156 real .desktop entries in the user's own KDE mimeapps.list read as missing. The 4KB single-line detail then buried both fail rows, so the operator saw only "do not log out until its failures are fixed" with no visible failure. Fixed: os-release skips at root "/", mime-handlers resolves against every XDG applications dir (snap and flatpak exports always included, not just what XDG_DATA_DIRS happens to carry), and the CLI abbreviates detail and prints a closing tally naming the failures.
        """
    observed_at git:a185a0043a662c2923503984557948f598ee5220
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-25
}

