record legeos.papercut.the-home-field-s-own-reflow-focus-ops-tests-are/1 : papercut {
    title "The Home Field's own reflow/focus/ops tests are thorough, but nothing…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The Home Field's own reflow/focus/ops tests are thorough, but nothing in the shell exercises a widget's declared regions through a real Ui with input — the field_screen harness always passes an empty widget map. So the session tile's rung assignment and its click routing had no coverage at all, and the inverted rung rule (Shut down at the floor, Log out hidden) was invisible to the suite. Teaching the harness to carry WidgetSnapshots would let every widget's controls be tested where they are actually drawn.
        """
    observed_at git:1d8611042a47c81297b8a2a3db2a2ff977f8a8cc
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-26
}

record legeos.papercut.the-installed-legeos-set-on-the-development/1 : papercut {
    title "The installed LegeOS set on the development machine was mixed-age: ten…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The installed LegeOS set on the development machine was mixed-age: ten of thirteen packages more than a day older than lege-shell, so an Aug-25 shell was calling Session.Lifecycle1 and current lege_shell_v1 requests against an Aug-22 sessiond and an Aug-23 compositor. Every symptom is silent and reads as an application bug. scripts/reinstall-legeos-desktop.sh apparently did not rebuild everything, or was run with --skip-build; `lege doctor`'s new package-ages check now catches the state, but the script itself should be re-examined.
        """
    observed_at git:e19b3524f6dacae9152e4d6b94a6d9891edee4f4
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-08-26
}

