    state verified
    statement """
        The working tree carried a body of in-flight work that did not compile (a borrow error in the portal's new dialog.rs) and had three failing shell tests, so `git status` looked like ordinary uncommitted progress while `cargo check` was broken. Running the gates before trusting a dirty tree cost a while; a pre-commit hook, or a note in the handoff that the tree is mid-change and red, would have said so up front.
        """
    observed_at git:06bf665f54b58b218e145fb66f8d4033e53e39bc
